+++ b/evidence/18-classification-semantics.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+FROZEN SOURCE QUERIES
+rg -n relevant definitions and operational rules in verification.k, semantics/core.k, semantics/list.k, semantics/int.k, semantics/subscript.k, semantics/sort.k, and prove.sh
+
+RELEVANT FROZEN RULES
+verification.k:
+- lines 11-22: three mergeThirdFrom base/step equations
+- lines 29-35: exact complete-result fold to sortThirdResult [simplification]
+- lines 37-39: guarded empty-result simplifier
+- lines 42-44: valSeqConcat associativity simplifier
+- line 47: valSeqConcat right-identity simplifier
+
+semantics/core.k:
+syntax ValSeq ::= .ValSeq | vCons(Val, ValSeq)
+syntax Int ::= vsLen(ValSeq) [function, total]
+rule vsLen(.ValSeq) => 0
+rule vsLen(vCons(_:Val, S:ValSeq)) => 1 +Int vsLen(S)
+
+semantics/list.k:
+syntax ValSeq ::= valSeqConcat(ValSeq, ValSeq) [function, total]
+rule valSeqConcat(.ValSeq, T:ValSeq) => T
+rule valSeqConcat(vCons(V:Val, S:ValSeq), T:ValSeq) => vCons(V, valSeqConcat(S, T))
+append mutates the result heap object with valSeqConcat(VS, vCons(V, .ValSeq)).
+
+semantics/int.k:
+rule applyBin("%", I1:Int, I2:Int) => pyMod(I1, I2)
+rule applyBin("//", I1:Int, I2:Int) => (I1 -Int pyMod(I1, I2)) /Int I2
+rule pyMod(I1:Int, I2:Int) => ((I1 %Int I2) +Int I2) %Int I2
+
+semantics/subscript.k:
+buildVS recurs by STEP while the index remains in bounds and otherwise returns .ValSeq.
+
+semantics/sort.k:
+sortVS is total/no-evaluators symbolically and has concrete insertion-sort equations for homogeneous integer and string sequences. sorted(list(VS)) allocates list(sortVS(VS)).
+
+prove.sh ORDERING
+verification.k is compiled once with all seven rules before either kprove command. There is no earlier proof of any exact domain-lemma rule against a module omitting it. Therefore none qualifies as PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA.
+
+INDEPENDENT CLASSIFICATION
+1. mergeThirdFrom base: DEFINITION. Terminating recurrence base, no operational cell.
+2. mergeThirdFrom divisible-by-three step: DEFINITION. Named summary recurrence; I increases and N-I decreases.
+3. mergeThirdFrom complementary step: DEFINITION. Exhaustive/disjoint complement of rule 2 for I<N.
+4. complete mergeThirdFrom -> sortThirdResult fold: DEFINITION. Exact named proof-term abbreviation; simplification is permitted for a definition.
+5. sortThirdResult empty under vsLen<=0: DOMAIN_LEMMA. Consequence of the summary/length algebra, installed without a prior proof; relevant to empty source input.
+6. valSeqConcat associativity: DOMAIN_LEMMA. Mathematical list law, installed without a prior proof; required to normalize repeated operational append in the loop invariant.
+7. valSeqConcat right identity: DOMAIN_LEMMA. Mathematical list law, installed without a prior proof; required at the accumulator boundary.
+
+COUNTS
+DEFINITION=4
+OPERATIONAL_RULE=0
+PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA=0
+DOMAIN_LEMMA=3
+Every simplification rule is DEFINITION or DOMAIN_LEMMA.
